    {
      "parameters": {
        "modelId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "gpt-5-mini",
          "mode": "list",
          "cachedResultName": "GPT-5-MINI"
        },
        "responses": {
          "values": [
            {
              "role": "system",
              "content": "You are Flow State, a non-medical personal well-being assistant.\n\nAnalyze the user's daily check-in together with their schedule and give a short, useful personal reflection.\n\nLook at:\n- energy\n- mental load\n- sleep duration\n- mood\n- what is on the user's mind\n- today's calendar workload\n\nDo not diagnose medical or mental-health conditions.\nDo not claim that one factor caused another.\nIf information is missing, do not invent it.\nGive practical, low-risk advice that is realistic for the user's schedule.\n\nRespond in a friendly and concise way with:\n1. Daily summary\n2. What is going well\n3. What to watch\n4. Advice for today"
            },
            {
              "content": "=Here is today's personal check-in:\n\nEnergy: {{ $('On form submission').item.json.Energy }}/10\nMental load: {{ $('On form submission').item.json.MentalLoad }}/10\nSleep: {{ $('On form submission').item.json.SleepHours }} hours\nMood: {{ $('On form submission').item.json.Mood }}\nOn my mind: {{ $('On form submission').item.json.OnMyMind }}\n\nCalendar information for the upcoming period:\n{{ JSON.stringify($('Get many events').all().map(item => ({\n  start: item.json.start,\n  end: item.json.end\n}))) }}\n\nUse this information to create today's Flow State review.\n\nWhen discussing the calendar:\n- consider how busy the schedule is\n- consider how much scheduled time there is\n- consider whether there are early or late events\n- do not repeat event titles or private calendar details\n- use the schedule only as context for practical advice\n\nIf calendar information is empty, still create the review using the personal check-in.\n\nDo not diagnose anything and do not claim that sleep, workload, mood, or another factor caused how the user feels.\n\n\n\nHISTORICAL DATA:\n{{ JSON.stringify($('Get row(s) in sheet').all().map(item => item.json)) }}\n\nUse the historical data above to identify patterns between sleep, energy, mental load, mood, and calendar workload. Only mention a pattern when the available data actually supports it. If there is not enough historical data yet, say that more check-ins are needed before reliable patterns can be identified."
            }
          ]
        },
